<OlspLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="https://olsp.profitandprivilege.com/blog/is-affiliate-marketing-a-scam/" tocLinks={tocLinks}>
<section id="answer"><h1>Is Affiliate Marketing a Scam? How to Evaluate an Offer</h1><p>Affiliate marketing itself is a performance-based referral model, not automatically a scam. Individual programs can still be poor value or misleading, so evaluate the specific offer instead of trusting the label.</p></section>
<GoldMasterQuote />
<section id="checklist"><h2>Five questions to ask</h2><ol><li>Is the price, refund policy, and recurring cost clear?</li><li>Can you identify the company and the product behind the claim?</li><li>Are earnings presented as typical, or only as exceptional examples?</li><li>Does the program explain what work produces a result?</li><li>Can you review independent information before paying?</li></ol><p>Walk away from pressure, secrecy, guaranteed income, or a requirement to recruit before understanding the product. Disclosure and realistic expectations are signs of a healthier decision process.</p></section>
<section id="source"><h2>Use the official explanation as a starting point</h2><p>The <a href="/olsp-livebinar/?utm_source=article&utm_medium=content&utm_campaign=affiliate_scam">OLSP Live Webinar</a> is the official presentation to review after reading the independent questions above. Treat it as information to evaluate, not a promise of income.</p></section>
</OlspLayout>
